WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.354
<v Examiner>Scenario one.

2
00:00:02.354 --> 00:00:06.710
<v Examiner>Mrs Harris is eighty-one and lives in aged residential care.

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.703
<v Examiner>She has asthma, atrial fibrillation and osteoarthritis.

4
00:00:10.703 --> 00:00:16.294
<v Examiner>She's prescribed a salbutamol inhaler, a hundred micrograms, two puffs P R N;

5
00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:18.908
<v Examiner>warfarin three milligrams P O nocte;

6
00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:25.442
<v Examiner>metoprolol forty-seven point five milligrams P O mane; and paracetamol one gram P O Q I D.

7
00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:27.765
<v Examiner>She takes nine medicines in all.

8
00:00:28.215 --> 00:00:32.253
Before the questions, read the chart like Joan wants.

9
00:00:32.253 --> 00:00:33.701
P R N, as required.

10
00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:34.768
P O, by mouth.

11
00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.987
Nocte, at night.

12
00:00:35.987 --> 00:00:37.587
Mane, in the morning.

13
00:00:37.587 --> 00:00:39.415
Q I D, four times a day.

14
00:00:39.865 --> 00:00:40.457
<v Examiner>Two marks.

15
00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:43.535
<v Examiner>What drug class is salbutamol, and how does it work?

16
00:00:43.985 --> 00:00:46.164
Salbutamol is a bronchodilator.

17
00:00:46.164 --> 00:00:51.998
It's a beta-2 agonist: it binds to the beta-2 receptors in the smooth muscle of the

18
00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:56.567
airways and relaxes it, so the airways open and the wheeze eases.

19
00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.043
Two marks, two lines.

20
00:00:58.493 --> 00:00:59.155
<v Examiner>Two marks.

21
00:00:59.155 --> 00:01:05.043
<v Examiner>Identify two assessments the nurse makes before and after Mrs Harris uses her salbutamol.

22
00:01:05.493 --> 00:01:09.136
Her respiratory rate, her work of breathing and her wheeze.

23
00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:11.914
And her oxygen saturation, or her heart rate,

24
00:01:11.914 --> 00:01:15.619
because salbutamol can cause a fast heart rate and a tremor.

25
00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:17.718
Before tells you why she needs it.

26
00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:19.509
After tells you if it worked.

27
00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:20.642
<v Examiner>Two marks.

28
00:01:20.642 --> 00:01:22.624
<v Examiner>Warfarin is an anticoagulant.

29
00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:28.705
<v Examiner>Identify one test used to monitor it, and one sign of bleeding you'd teach her to report.

30
00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:33.907
The test is the I N R, a blood test of how long the blood takes to clot.

31
00:01:33.907 --> 00:01:39.715
Signs of bleeding: unusual bruising, bleeding gums, blood in her urine, or black stools.

32
00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:40.810
<v Examiner>Two marks.

33
00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:46.224
<v Examiner>Define polypharmacy, and give one strategy to support Mrs Harris with her medicines.

34
00:01:46.674 --> 00:01:51.127
Polypharmacy is taking many medicines at once, often five or more,

35
00:01:51.127 --> 00:01:55.378
which raises the risk of interactions, side effects and errors.

36
00:01:55.378 --> 00:01:59.629
A strategy: blister packs or a pill organiser with visual aids.

37
00:01:59.629 --> 00:02:02.396
That was the answer on her formative two.

38
00:02:02.396 --> 00:02:04.487
Or ask for a medication review.

39
00:02:04.937 --> 00:02:05.561
<v Examiner>One mark.

40
00:02:05.561 --> 00:02:10.825
<v Examiner>Identify one age-related change that may mean Mrs Harris needs a lower dose.

41
00:02:11.275 --> 00:02:12.867
Decreased renal function.

42
00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:16.434
Her kidneys excrete drugs more slowly, so they build up.

43
00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.873
That's her formative two, question one, word for word.

44
00:02:20.323 --> 00:02:22.143
Scenario one, Mrs Harris.

45
00:02:22.143 --> 00:02:28.041
Salbutamol: a bronchodilator, a beta-2 agonist that relaxes airway smooth muscle.

46
00:02:28.041 --> 00:02:33.720
Assess respiratory rate, wheeze, saturations and heart rate, before and after.

47
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:40.274
Warfarin: monitor the I N R; report bruising, bleeding gums, blood in urine, black stools.

48
00:02:40.274 --> 00:02:45.225
Polypharmacy: many medicines at once; blister packs and visual aids.

49
00:02:45.225 --> 00:02:48.065
Older adults: decreased renal function.
